{"type":"text","timestamp":1794585151156,"sessionID":"ses_e2a666a64ffe0MO4YglSgi7g6l","part":{"id":"prt_1d59c33fd0013l4wHkKOH0Yi3Y","sessionID":"ses_e2a666a64ffe0MO4YglSgi7g6l","messageID":"msg_1d59c2c83001Hd0TLmxqTG8L44","type":"text","text":"T030 is done.\n\n## Files written\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-helper-handoff.vitest.ts` — added three expectations inside `reads a tool that does not show up as a strong cue`: `it doesn't appear to cover the routing case` → `null`, `don't show up-to-date entries only` → `null`, `the linter does not appear in the tool list` → `strong`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts` — first alternative of `STRONG_PROBLEM_CUE` now uses `show(?:s|ing)? up(?![-\\\\w])|appear(?:s|ing)?(?! to\\\\b)`, and the cue comment gained one sentence: `\"appear to\" states an impression and \"up-to-date\" is a compound, so neither says a tool is missing.`\n\n## Verify output\nTest-first run (before the regex change) failed as required. Vitest stops at the first failed assertion in a block, so I put each new `null` case first in turn to observe both:\n\n```\nAssertionError: expected 'strong' to be null   (it doesn't appear to cover the routing case)\nAssertionError: expected 'strong' to be null   (don't show up-to-date entries only)\n```\n\nFinal state:\n\n```\n$ npm run typecheck\n> typecheck\n> .../tsc --noEmit --composite false -p tsconfig.build.json\nTC_EXIT=0\n\n$ env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/doctor-helper-handoff.vitest.ts tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts tests/doctor-routing-slice.vitest.ts\n\n Test Files  3 passed (3)\n      Tests  25 passed (25)\n   Duration  3.10s\n```\n\n## Not done\n- `T030` checkbox left unticked, as instructed.\n- Spec-folder `validate.sh --strict` not run: the task names its own verify and other workers' files are mid-edit.","time":{"start":1794585146365,"end":1794585151156}}}
